---
title: "Tooltips"
---

Tooltips display additional information for cells and column headers on hover, keyboard focus or touch.

Use `tooltip: true` for the common case where the tooltip should match the displayed cell value: `valueFormatted` when present, otherwise `value`, whatever their source — a [Value Getter](./value-getters/), [Aggregation](./aggregation/) or a [Calculated Column](./calculated-columns/). A string value shows fixed text instead.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    columnDefs: [
        { field: 'athlete', tooltip: true },
        { field: 'country', tooltip: 'The country the athlete represents' },
    ],
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Cell Tooltips" name="tooltips" /%}

{% apiDocumentation source="column-properties/properties.json" section="tooltips" names=["tooltip"] /%}

`tooltip: false` disables cell tooltip content supplied by `tooltip`, `tooltipField` or `tooltipValueGetter`. Tooltips registered at runtime with [`setTooltip`](#dynamic-tooltips) and grid-owned validation or formula error tooltips remain available.

The grid's own controls show [Built-in Control Tooltips](./tooltips-built-in/). For tooltip behaviour and customisation, see:

- [Show and Hide Delay](./tooltips-show-hide/) {% #show-and-hide-delay %}
- [Keyboard Focus](./tooltips-show-hide/#keyboard-focus) {% #keyboard-focus %}
- [Positioning](./tooltips-positioning/) {% #positioning %}
- [Arrows](./tooltips-positioning/#arrows) {% #arrows %}
- [Custom Component](./component-tooltip/) {% #custom-component %}
- [Interactive Tooltips](./tooltips-show-hide/#interactive-tooltips) {% #interactive-tooltips %}
- [Mouse Tracking](./tooltips-positioning/#mouse-tracking) {% #mouse-tracking %}
- [Touch Devices](./tooltips-show-hide/#touch-devices) {% #touch-devices %}

## Header Tooltips

`headerTooltip` accepts the same value forms. With `headerTooltip: true`, the displayed header name is used. Column groups accept `headerTooltip` too.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    columnDefs: [
        { field: 'athlete', headerTooltip: true },
        { field: 'age', headerTooltip: 'The athlete\'s age at the time of the games' },
    ],
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Header Tooltips" name="header-tooltips" /%}

{% apiDocumentation source="column-properties/properties.json" section="header" names=["headerTooltip"] /%}

## Tooltip Callback

Pass a callback to `tooltip` or `headerTooltip` to generate content dynamically. Cell callbacks receive `TooltipCallbackParams`, with the underlying cell value and row data; header callbacks receive `HeaderTooltipCallbackParams`, where `value` is the displayed header name. `valueFormatted` contains the formatted source value when available.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    columnDefs: [
        { field: 'athlete', tooltip: (params) => params.data.country },
    ],
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tooltip Callback" name="tooltip-callback" /%}

{% expandingSection headerText="TooltipCallbackParams" %}
{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="TooltipCallbackParams" /%}
{% /expandingSection %}

## Blank Values

Tooltips are not shown for the missing values `undefined`, `null` and `''` (empty string). To display a tooltip for a missing value, use a callback that returns non-empty content.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Blank Values" name="blank-values" /%}

## Tooltips for Truncated Text

Set `tooltipShowMode: 'whenTruncated'` to show tooltips only when the hovered or focused text is truncated. Built-in control tooltips do not require truncated text, except floating-filter value previews, which show only when truncated.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    tooltipShowMode: 'whenTruncated',
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tooltips" name="tooltip-show-mode" /%}

{% note %}
`tooltipShowMode = 'whenTruncated'` has no effect when using Browser Tooltips, as Browser Tooltips are controlled by the browser and not the grid.
{% /note %}

## Dynamic Tooltips

Custom cell renderers and header components can register tooltip content at runtime with the `setTooltip` method on their params. `tooltip: false` and `headerTooltip: false` do not disable these. See [Cell Components](./component-cell-renderer/#dynamic-tooltips), [Header Components](./column-headers-components/#dynamic-tooltips) and [Column Groups](./column-groups/#dynamic-tooltips).

## Row Groups

When a column is grouped, the generated group column inherits `tooltip`, `tooltipComponent` and `tooltipComponentParams` from the underlying column's [Column Definition](./column-definitions/), consistent with how `valueFormatter` is inherited. Cell tooltip properties set on `autoGroupColumnDef` apply to leaf rows only; `headerTooltip` still applies to the group column header.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Row Group Tooltip" name="rowgroups-tooltip" /%}

### Grouped Column Headers

With `groupDisplayType: 'multipleColumns'`, each generated group column header inherits the `headerTooltip` from its underlying column `colDef`.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Grouped Column Header Tooltip" name="rowgroups-header-tooltip" /%}

### Full Width Group Rows

With `groupDisplayType: 'groupRows'`, full-width group rows inherit their tooltips from the underlying column `colDef`.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Full Width Group Row Tooltip" name="rowgroups-fullwidth-tooltip" /%}

### Aggregated Cells

When a group row displays an aggregated value in a data column, hovering that cell shows a tooltip for the aggregated value, not the underlying row data.

## Browser Tooltip

Set `enableBrowserTooltips: true` to use the browser's native tooltips instead of the grid's Tooltip Component. Custom components, delays, positioning and the immediate-focus behaviour do not apply; built-in controls fall back to native `title` hints.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    enableBrowserTooltips: true,
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Default Browser Tooltip" name="default-tooltip" /%}
